Management cluster mgmt/mgmt
  record   ob-management  one delivery profile per variant (8): each sends its variant's releases to its one cluster

In ConfigHub
  4 Targets in ob-targets, one per cluster, on a server-hosted worker
  3 components, each one base, 8 variants, 1 management record
  13 Spaces and 8 Links, one tying each unit of a class base or a variant to its upstream (check your organization's quotas for both first)
  first rollout: ingress-nginx in 1 stage, kyverno in 2 stages, kyverno-policies in 2 stages; one approval per stage, one release per variant

Note: kyverno's chart kyverno has 11 Helm hooks for upgrade, delete or test, among them Jobs kyverno-migrate-resources, kyverno-rm-webhooks, kyverno-scale-to-zero. They are left out, as cub helm leaves them out, because only Helm runs them.

Live on your management cluster: ingress-nginx, kyverno, kyverno-policies. Each delivery profile deploys the same objects to the same cluster. apply also writes handover.sh, which steps each live profile aside without removing anything, so the delivery profiles carry on alone; run it after apply.sh. See "If your profiles are live" in docs/user/onboard-your-sveltos-fleet.md.

Next: cub sveltos apply <the same input and options> --out <dir>, read <dir>/apply.sh, then run it.

