Helm still records release ingress-nginx on prod-eu, prod-us, though ConfigHub manages its objects now, so a helm uninstall there would remove them. Remove the record, which leaves the objects, on each of those clusters: kubectl -n ingress-nginx delete secret -l owner=helm,name=ingress-nginx
Helm still records release kyverno on staging-eu, prod-eu, prod-us, though ConfigHub manages its objects now, so a helm uninstall there would remove them. Remove the record, which leaves the objects, on each of those clusters: kubectl -n kyverno delete secret -l owner=helm,name=kyverno
ConfigMap default/kyverno-policies is no longer read; ConfigHub holds its objects. Delete it when you are ready: kubectl delete configmap -n default kyverno-policies

